<title>UK: NatWest says will issue $500 mln debt.</title>
<headline>NatWest says will issue $500 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Westminster Bank Plc said in a statement on Monday it planned to issue $500 million of subordinated debt.</p>
<p>The reset notes, which will qualify as upper tier two capital under Bank of England guidelines, will pay a fixed rate of interest for the first 10.5 years. Thereafter, they will pay a margin over six-month Libor.</p>
<p>The notes will be callable at par after 10.5 years.</p>
<p>Final terms will be set in the near future, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
